{"id": "EUVD-2026-102351", "enisaUuid": "49088a4d-316f-38f3-a22f-7b7d23efb546", "description": "AdPlug through 2.4 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in src/xsm.cpp that allows attackers to read before note_table by supplying a negative note index. Attackers can craft an XSM file with the ofTAZ! signature and a song byte of 0x80 or higher, causing a global-buffer-overflow read during playback that may crash affected applications.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:14:06", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/adplug-ksm-note-loop-databuf-oob-write", "https://github.com/adplug/adplug/blob/e491e382479ed2246f124c96c70d94561dce59b9/src/xsm.cpp#L86-L134", "https://github.com/adplug/adplug", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/adplug-through-2.4-out-of-bounds-read-via-cxsmplayer-play-note-in-xsm-files"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5f64-5878-cg28", "CVE-2026-110876"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d2943931-344c-3eff-ac69-a9bad122d5d2", "product": {"name": "adplug", "vendor": {"name": "adplug"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "12090dc8-f2d2-307c-bde8-c47d7eeb9b68", "vendor": {"name": "adplug"}}], "isExploited": false}